{"id":"1c3334bd8714f888","group":"93","path":"93/93-thm-lowenheim-skolem.md","title":"Lowenheim-Skolem Theorem","display":"Lowenheim-Skolem Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Algebraizable Logics","book_abbrev":"93","label":"93-thm-lowenheim-skolem","aliases":["93-thm-lowenheim-skolem"],"display":"Lowenheim-Skolem Theorem","depends_on":["[[93-df-first-order-language]]","[[93-df-first-order-structure]]","[[93-df-cardinality]]","[[93-df-elementary-substructure]]","[[93-df-elementary-extension]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Algebraizable Logics"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"93"},{"key":"label","html":"93-thm-lowenheim-skolem"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>93-thm-lowenheim-skolem</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"Lowenheim-Skolem Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"cc9bc888c7dda430\" href=\"?note=cc9bc888c7dda430\" title=\"93-df-first-order-language\">93-df-first-order-language</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"0ce709e0d2857990\" href=\"?note=0ce709e0d2857990\" title=\"93-df-first-order-structure\">93-df-first-order-structure</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"1734624324342672\" href=\"?note=1734624324342672\" title=\"93-df-cardinality\">93-df-cardinality</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"1a1e430b602adf49\" href=\"?note=1a1e430b602adf49\" title=\"93-df-elementary-substructure\">93-df-elementary-substructure</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"de37e41e6c0ca2b6\" href=\"?note=de37e41e6c0ca2b6\" title=\"93-df-elementary-extension\">93-df-elementary-extension</a></span></div>"}],"html":"<h1 id=\"thm-lowenheim-skolem-—-Lowenheim-Skolem-Theorem\">thm-lowenheim-skolem — Lowenheim-Skolem Theorem</h1>\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{FOLang}_{93}(\\mathcal L)\">\\(\\mathrm{FOLang}_{93}(\\mathcal L)\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{FOStruct}_{93}(\\mathfrak A,\\mathcal L)\">\\(\\mathrm{FOStruct}_{93}(\\mathfrak A,\\mathcal L)\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A=|\\mathfrak A|\">\\(A=|\\mathfrak A|\\)</span> is infinite.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\lambda,\\mu\">\\(\\lambda,\\mu\\)</span> are infinite cardinals; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CardLe}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{CardLe}_{93}\\)</span> explicitly compares the nonlogical-symbol set, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\lambda\">\\(\\lambda\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\">\\(A\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mu\">\\(\\mu\\)</span> by injections.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Sym}_{93}(\\mathcal L)\">\\(\\operatorname{Sym}_{93}(\\mathcal L)\\)</span> is the sourced full nonlogical-symbol set of <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"cc9bc888c7dda430\" href=\"?note=cc9bc888c7dda430\" title=\"93-df-first-order-language\">93-df-first-order-language</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ElemSub}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{ElemSub}_{93}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ElemExt}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{ElemExt}_{93}\\)</span> are the predicates of the cited definitions.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CardEq}\">\\(\\mathrm{CardEq}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CardLe}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{CardLe}_{93}\\)</span> are the equipotence and cardinal-comparison predicates of <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"1734624324342672\" href=\"?note=1734624324342672\" title=\"93-df-cardinality\">93-df-cardinality</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Finite}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{Finite}_{93}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{InfCard}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{InfCard}_{93}\\)</span> are the finite-set and infinite-cardinal predicates sourced by <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"1734624324342672\" href=\"?note=1734624324342672\" title=\"93-df-cardinality\">93-df-cardinality</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}lowenheim\\text{-}skolem}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{FOLang}_{93}(\\mathcal L)\\land\\mathrm{FOStruct}_{93}(\\mathfrak A,\\mathcal L)\n\\land A=|\\mathfrak A|\\land\\neg\\mathrm{Finite}_{93}(A)\n\\land\\mathrm{InfCard}_{93}(\\lambda)\\land\\mathrm{InfCard}_{93}(\\mu)\n\\land\\mathrm{CardLe}_{93}(\\operatorname{Sym}_{93}(\\mathcal L),\\lambda)\n\\land\\mathrm{CardLe}_{93}(\\lambda,A)\n\\land\\mathrm{CardLe}_{93}(A,\\mu)\\\\\n&amp;\\to\\Bigl(\\Bigl[\\exists\\mathfrak B\\;\\bigl(\n\\mathrm{ElemSub}_{93}(\\mathfrak B,\\mathfrak A;\\mathcal L)\\land\n\\mathrm{CardEq}(|\\mathfrak B|,\\lambda)\\bigr)\\Bigr]\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{2em}\\land\\Bigl[\\exists\\mathfrak C\\;\\bigl(\n\\mathrm{ElemExt}_{93}(\\mathfrak C,\\mathfrak A;\\mathcal L)\\land\n\\mathrm{CardEq}(|\\mathfrak C|,\\mu)\\bigr)\\Bigr]\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}lowenheim\\text{-}skolem}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{FOLang}_{93}(\\mathcal L)\\land\\mathrm{FOStruct}_{93}(\\mathfrak A,\\mathcal L)\n\\land A=|\\mathfrak A|\\land\\neg\\mathrm{Finite}_{93}(A)\n\\land\\mathrm{InfCard}_{93}(\\lambda)\\land\\mathrm{InfCard}_{93}(\\mu)\n\\land\\mathrm{CardLe}_{93}(\\operatorname{Sym}_{93}(\\mathcal L),\\lambda)\n\\land\\mathrm{CardLe}_{93}(\\lambda,A)\n\\land\\mathrm{CardLe}_{93}(A,\\mu)\\\\\n&amp;\\to\\Bigl(\\Bigl[\\exists\\mathfrak B\\;\\bigl(\n\\mathrm{ElemSub}_{93}(\\mathfrak B,\\mathfrak A;\\mathcal L)\\land\n\\mathrm{CardEq}(|\\mathfrak B|,\\lambda)\\bigr)\\Bigr]\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{2em}\\land\\Bigl[\\exists\\mathfrak C\\;\\bigl(\n\\mathrm{ElemExt}_{93}(\\mathfrak C,\\mathfrak A;\\mathcal L)\\land\n\\mathrm{CardEq}(|\\mathfrak C|,\\mu)\\bigr)\\Bigr]\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>The first conjunct is downward Löwenheim–Skolem and the second is upward Löwenheim–Skolem. The injection chain replaces an undeclared cardinality-function notation. Separate cardinals are required: an elementary extension containing <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\">\\(A\\)</span> cannot have size below that of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\">\\(A\\)</span>.</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"thm-lowenheim-skolem-—-Lowenheim-Skolem-Theorem","text":"thm-lowenheim-skolem — Lowenheim-Skolem Theorem","level":1},{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"93-df-first-order-language","status":"resolved","id":"cc9bc888c7dda430","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-first-order-language]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-first-order-structure","status":"resolved","id":"0ce709e0d2857990","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-first-order-structure]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-cardinality","status":"resolved","id":"1734624324342672","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-cardinality]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-elementary-substructure","status":"resolved","id":"1a1e430b602adf49","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-elementary-substructure]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-elementary-extension","status":"resolved","id":"de37e41e6c0ca2b6","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-elementary-extension]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-first-order-language","status":"resolved","id":"cc9bc888c7dda430","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{Sym}_{93}(\\mathcal L)$ is the sourced full nonlogical-symbol set of [[93-df-first-order-language]].","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-cardinality","status":"resolved","id":"1734624324342672","anchor":"ref-7","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{CardEq}$ and $\\mathrm{CardLe}_{93}$ are the equipotence and cardinal-comparison predicates of [[93-df-cardinality]].","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-cardinality","status":"resolved","id":"1734624324342672","anchor":"ref-8","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Finite}_{93}$ and $\\mathrm{InfCard}_{93}$ are the finite-set and infinite-cardinal predicates sourced by [[93-df-cardinality]].","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\mathrm{FOLang}_{93}(\\mathcal L)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{FOStruct}_{93}(\\mathfrak A,\\mathcal L)","display":false},{"tex":"A=|\\mathfrak A|","display":false},{"tex":"\\lambda,\\mu","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{CardLe}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\lambda","display":false},{"tex":"A","display":false},{"tex":"\\mu","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{Sym}_{93}(\\mathcal L)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ElemSub}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ElemExt}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{CardEq}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{CardLe}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Finite}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{InfCard}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}lowenheim\\text{-}skolem}\\vdash{}&\n\\mathrm{FOLang}_{93}(\\mathcal L)\\land\\mathrm{FOStruct}_{93}(\\mathfrak A,\\mathcal L)\n\\land A=|\\mathfrak A|\\land\\neg\\mathrm{Finite}_{93}(A)\n\\land\\mathrm{InfCard}_{93}(\\lambda)\\land\\mathrm{InfCard}_{93}(\\mu)\n\\land\\mathrm{CardLe}_{93}(\\operatorname{Sym}_{93}(\\mathcal L),\\lambda)\n\\land\\mathrm{CardLe}_{93}(\\lambda,A)\n\\land\\mathrm{CardLe}_{93}(A,\\mu)\\\\\n&\\to\\Bigl(\\Bigl[\\exists\\mathfrak B\\;\\bigl(\n\\mathrm{ElemSub}_{93}(\\mathfrak B,\\mathfrak A;\\mathcal L)\\land\n\\mathrm{CardEq}(|\\mathfrak B|,\\lambda)\\bigr)\\Bigr]\\\\\n&\\hspace{2em}\\land\\Bigl[\\exists\\mathfrak C\\;\\bigl(\n\\mathrm{ElemExt}_{93}(\\mathfrak C,\\mathfrak A;\\mathcal L)\\land\n\\mathrm{CardEq}(|\\mathfrak C|,\\mu)\\bigr)\\Bigr]\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"A","display":false},{"tex":"A","display":false}],"bytes":2258,"backlinks":[],"outgoing":["cc9bc888c7dda430","0ce709e0d2857990","1734624324342672","1a1e430b602adf49","de37e41e6c0ca2b6"]}